From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: iertutil: parse Windows.Foundation.Uri with urlmon's IUri

Windows.Foundation.Uri stored the raw string and nothing else: every property
but RawUri returned E_NOTIMPL, AbsoluteUri echoed the input, and
CreateWithRelativeUri and CombineUri were stubs. Anything that asks a Uri for
its host, path or query failed -- ResourceLoader's GetStringForReference
(ms-resource:///Map/Key) among them, and HTTP clients building requests.

Parse with urlmon's RFC 3986 IUri (CreateUri) at creation, and answer each
property from the matching Uri_PROPERTY: AbsoluteUri (canonical),
DisplayUri, Domain, Extension, Fragment, Host, Password, Path, Query,
SchemeName, UserName and Port. Equals compares canonical forms;
CombineUri and CreateWithRelativeUri use CoInternetCombineUrlEx. A string
that is not an absolute URI is E_INVALIDARG, as on Windows. QueryParsed stays
unimplemented.

